7d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-126479/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126479" :question/id #uuid "ada2c6aa-e1cf-5c5d-97a8-778452c8133f" :question/math-academy-id "q-126479" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $C$ is upper triangular\n- $C$ is lower triangular\n- ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of $C$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $C$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${C}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126479/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126479"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74318/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "08e40fd7-c8ee-582b-a6e1-bd1cb96da954" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74318/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9562542f-892f-5d59-b7db-7e1ede55634c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74318/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c